-- title:
--   Twisted Frobenius fixed places on the Drinfeld curve: N(1,η)=q+1
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and a field $k$ that is an algebra over $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}=$ `GaloisField q 2` and is algebraically closed, and assume the coordinate ring `CoordRing q k`, the quotient of $k[X_0,X_1]$ by the ideal generated by `drinfeldPoly q k - 1`, is a domain; let `drinfeldFunctionField q k` be its fraction field $F$, and write $X$, $Y$ for the images in $F$ of the two coordinate classes `x q k`, `y q k`. Let $\varphi : F \to F$ be a $k$-algebra endomorphism whose underlying ring homomorphism is integral and which satisfies $\varphi(X) = X^{q^2}$ and $\varphi(Y) = Y^{q^2}$. Let $\eta$ be a $(q+1)$-st root of unity in $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$, viewed as an element of `rootsOfUnity (q + 1) (GaloisField q 2)`, and assume $\eta \neq -1$ in $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$. Then the set of places $w$ of $F$ over $k$ — a place being a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $k$, distinct from $F$ itself and a principal ideal ring — such that the place `Place.restrictAlong φ hφi w`, whose valuation subring is the preimage $\varphi^{-1}(\mathcal{O}_w)$, equals the translate of $w$ by the automorphism of $F$ obtained by applying `hFunctionFieldAction q k` to the element of `hSubgroup q` attached to $\eta$ by `one_mem_hSubgroup_of_mem`, has cardinality exactly $q + 1$.
--
--   This is the twisted-Frobenius (Deligne–Lusztig) fixed-place count $N(1,\eta)$ for the Drinfeld curve $xy^q - x^qy = 1$, for a central twist $\eta \in \mu_{q+1}$ other than $-1$: the $q^2$-power Frobenius correspondence composed with the twist has exactly the $q+1$ places at infinity as fixed places, the affine contribution vanishing. It is used in the computation of the dimension of the $\eta$-eigenspace of the rational Tate module of the curve, in [`DrinfeldCurve.finrank_eigenspace_rootsOfUnity_rationalTateModule_eq`](thm.html#DrinfeldCurve.finrank_eigenspace_rootsOfUnity_rationalTateModule_eq).
